      "authoringHints": {
        "styles": "Every style falls back to the app theme, so set only what the design needs to blend in (its accent, surfaces, borders and text colours), taking colours from the app theme or brand, never the defaults of another product. Radii and sizes are px. Styles are the way to restyle a pack widget: a cssClass only takes effect with workspace Custom styles, and Tailwind class names the pack does not already use are not compiled, so do not rely on either; for a one-off visual a style cannot express, use an Html component. Bind loadingState to the query's isLoading (each widget draws a skeleton or spinner in its own shape); tooltip shows on hover.",
        "usage": "Things with a face as cards instead of table rows: recipes, products, listings, rooms, people, tasks. imageField when rows have photos (without it the cards have no picture area; never draw an SVG or data: image as a picture), badgeField for a state, descriptionField for a line of detail, metaFields for 2 or 3 facts ('prep:{} min, serves:Serves'). More on a card: badgeFields for extra chips ('diet, spice', up to 4 with badgeField), eyebrowField for a small caps line above the title (a category, a city, a team, a code), avatarField for an owner or host (a photo URL, else initials), progressField for a percentage bar (a project, a goal, a course). layout 'row' puts the image left of the text: listings, people and a compact catalogue in two columns. onCardClicked with selectedItem opens details. About 300px per row with images, 150 without or in rows."
      }
